# Postgres connection string. Required — there is no default, and the service
# refuses to start without it rather than silently using an empty database.
# A connection must use TLS (#1695): a URL with no sslmode gets sslmode=require, and on a deploy
# (RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT_NAME or PRODUCTION set) a weaker sslmode refuses the boot. The local
# development database (`docker compose --profile localdb up -d postgres`) speaks no TLS, so its URL
# turns it off explicitly — which only a local run allows:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://reli:reli@localhost:5432/reli?sslmode=disable

# Google sign-in for the OAuth 2.1 authorization server at /oauth/*, which a claude.ai connector
# authorises against: the JWT it mints is the only credential /mcp accepts, so /mcp answers 401 to
# every request until SECRET_KEY is set. The session cookie it sets is likewise the only credential
# /api accepts — #1471 retired the HTTP Basic password that used to sit beside it. Human-
# provisioned: every one defaults to empty, empty closes the sign-in (501 naming what is missing, no
# JWT accepted) and never stops the boot, so /healthz stays green and a missing secret cannot roll a
# deploy back. SECRET_KEY signs the JWTs — at least 32 random bytes (shorter counts as empty), e.g.
# `python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"`. ALLOWED_EMAILS is the
# comma-separated list of Google accounts allowed in; empty admits nobody. GOOGLE_AUTH_REDIRECT_URI
# is https://<host>/api/auth/google/callback, authorised verbatim on the OAuth client below, which
# must be a Web application client for this. RELI_BASE_URL is derived from it when empty.
# SECRET_KEY=
# ALLOWED_EMAILS=
# GOOGLE_AUTH_REDIRECT_URI=
# RELI_BASE_URL=

# The Web application OAuth client that identifies Reli to Google during a sign-in. Since #1488
# deleted the Calendar and Gmail readers this is the only Google credential Reli holds. Leaving
# these unset is safe — Reli boots and /healthz stays green; only the sign-in is closed.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Logging level
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Sentry error monitoring (optional — empty DSN disables it)
# SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0.2

# --- Staging, only for the host that runs docker-compose.staging.yml ---
# Kept distinct from DATABASE_URL so staging never points at production data.
# Its postgres-staging speaks no TLS, hence sslmode=disable; this compose file sets no PRODUCTION,
# only HIDE_API_DOCS to take its API docs offline (#1720).
# STAGING_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://reli:CHANGEME@postgres-staging:5432/reli_staging?sslmode=disable
# STAGING_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Cloudflare Zero Trust tunnel token — host infrastructure, not read by the app.
# Create tunnel at: https://one.dash.cloudflare.com → Networks → Tunnels
# Set the tunnel's public hostname to point to http://reli:8000
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=your_cf_tunnel_token_here
